From e14b22e70e070d3d6a0f54e9a190101eece911cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Malard <malard@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:11:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Video][FileItem] Give a videodb:// item its file when
 LoadDetails() fills it

CFileItem::LoadDetails() fills an item named by its videodb:// path from
the library record and merges that in with UpdateInfo(). Until
1d9f10fb53 the merge also copied the record's file into the item's
dynamic path, because GetDynPath() answers the path of an item that has
no dynamic path of its own. Nothing else on that route resolves the
path, so since then the player has been handed the videodb:// path
itself, and PlayMedia(videodb://movies/titles/<id>) stopped playing.

LoadDetails() now sets the dynamic path from the record. An item that
already has one keeps it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 xbmc/FileItem.cpp          |  4 +++
 xbmc/test/TestFileItem.cpp | 66 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 70 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/FileItem.cpp b/xbmc/FileItem.cpp
index 7f7e6e5..2e98908 100644
--- a/xbmc/FileItem.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/FileItem.cpp
@@ -2214,6 +2214,10 @@ bool CFileItem::LoadDetails()
     {
       const CFileItem loadedItem{*tag};
       UpdateInfo(loadedItem);
+
+      // The record names the file a videodb:// path plays, and nothing later resolves it
+      if (!HasDynPath())
+        SetDynPath(loadedItem.GetPath());
     }
     return ret;
   }
diff --git a/xbmc/test/TestFileItem.cpp b/xbmc/test/TestFileItem.cpp
index 7277f85..340bb25 100644
--- a/xbmc/test/TestFileItem.cpp
